      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`kill_process_tree` in the multimodal runtime catches `psutil.NoSuchProcess` when constructing the parent handle, but the parent can exit before `children(recursive=True)`. Return when it disappears during enumeration so teardown does not raise this race. The SRT helper is a separate owner and already guards the same lookup-to-enumeration race.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Catch the parent disappearing during child enumeration.\n- Retain the focused regression in the current process test file, sharing the upstream `unittest.mock` imports.\n- Merge main `834bfe4ef0` to resolve the test import conflict. Keep all upstream process reaping and GC-deferral behavior/tests.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nCurrent merged head: the complete standalone `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_process.py` passes all nine tests on Linux/Python 3.12.3 with psutil 7.1.3, including real process-tree cleanup, skipped-PID preservation, fork/GC restoration and the parent-exit race. No skips. Replacing only the production module with pinned main makes the parent-exit regression fail with `psutil.NoSuchProcess`; candidate bytes were restored and verified.\n\n```bash\npython python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_process.py -v\n```\n\nAll applicable repository pre-commit hooks pass on both changed files, plus `git diff --check`. Windows hooks use a task-local `python3` launcher pointing to native Python; process/fork tests run on the authorized Linux host. This is standalone unittest evidence; full multimodal pytest/conftest and accelerator suites were not run. No model output changes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this changes process teardown only.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with applicable pre-commit hooks\n- [x] Add a focused regression and retain upstream process/GC tests\n- [x] Documentation and performance benchmarks are not applicable to this cleanup fix\n- [x] Keep the change within the existing SGLang style\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39198126301](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39198126301)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39198126237](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39198126237)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39198126224](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39198126224)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n\n### Hosted CI gate\n\nHosted CI is currently blocked at the label gate: `run-ci` is missing (the extra workflow also requires `run-ci-extra`). This contributor account has no triage/write permission to enable those labels. Could a maintainer enable the appropriate CI runs? The lint workflow is running separately.\n",
